,"evidence":"bring a claim regarding the allegation to the Office for Civil Rights of the Department of Health and Human Services, for expedited resolution","evidence_verified":true,"key":"fiscal","score":25},{"assessment":"Imposes new nationwide nondiscrimination mandates, mandatory policy modifications, and structured enforcement pathways across the entire organ transplant system.","evidence":"A covered entity shall make reasonable modifications to policies or practices... if such modifications are necessary to make an organ transplant or related services available","evidence_verified":false,"key":"scope","score":65},{"assessment":"Establishes permanent statutory prohibitions and ongoing regulatory obligations for healthcare entities.","evidence":"The provisions of this Act... apply to an organ transplant, also apply to the evaluation and listing... and to the organ transplant and post-organ-transplant treatment","evidence_verified":false,"key":"duration","score":70}],"missing_information":["Specific cost estimates for implementing compliance or handling civil rights claims are absent."],"rationale":"Prohibits healthcare providers and organ networks from discriminating against individuals with disabilities in organ transplants, introduces requirements for reasonable policy modifications, and establishes civil rights enforcement claims.","score":60},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T21:45:34+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1520/BILLS-119hr1520rfs.htm"]},"introduced_date":"2025-02-24","is_demo":false,"label":"H.R. 1520","latest_action":{"date":"2025-06-24","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions."},"members":[{"chamber":"House","district":"3","id":"C001039","name":"Rep. Cammack, Kat","party":"R","role":"sponsor","state":"FL"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-24","district":"6","id":"D000